 "_note": "The DSX Scene COLLIDE corpus (dsx-scene.md P5): opt-in collisions as data. collide=\"sphere\" uses the node's bounding sphere (the picking-sphere law verbatim: center = world origin, radius scaled by the largest world basis column); collide=\"box\" uses the world AABB of the node's local half extents (box: size/2 · sphere: radius · plane: [w/2, h/2, 0]) — the 8 corners transformed and folded to min/max. THE DEPTH LAWS: sphere↔sphere depth = ra + rb − |ca − cb|; box↔box needs every axis overlap > 0, depth = min axis overlap; sphere↔box clamps the center to the box — outside: depth = r − dist, center inside: depth = r + nearest-face distance. A pair overlaps only when depth > 0 — exact touch is NOT a contact. THE ENTER LAW (track cases): on:collide fires when a pair STARTS overlapping (both directions: {id, other, depth}) and fires again only after the pair has separated. THE RUNTIME LAW (surface-tested): the pass runs after each RENDERED frame while at least one on:collide handler is authored — nothing moves without a render, so a static scene pays nothing. Floats 6 decimals, tolerance 1.5e-6; numbers from an independent scratch implementation. Runners: TS (per-PR). Kotlin/Swift are the NAMED P5 follow-up.",
